Problems identified in the code:
Loop condition bug: i <= scores.length should be i < scores.length.With <= it goes one extra iteration and scores[3] is undefined, so total becomes NaN.No return: The function only console.log(average) but doesn't return it. So const result will be undefined.Corrected version:javascriptfunction calculateAverage(scores) {
let total = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < scores.length; i++) { // fixed: < not <=
    total += scores[i];
}
let average = total / scores.length;
return average; // fixed: return instead of console.log
}

